# Product Requirements Document: Akamai Synthetic Release Gate

| | |
|---|---|
| **Product** | Akamai Synthetic Release Gate (repo: `synthetics-tests`) |
| **Document type** | Functional PRD |
| **Status** | Reflects the implemented system as of 2026-11-07 (single-profile v1, multi-app model from `PLAN-APPS.md`) |
| **Scope** | Functional behaviour only. How the capabilities are presented is out of scope for this document and follows from the requirements below. |

---

## 1. Summary

Akamai property changes are activated first on the Akamai **staging** network and then on **production**. Before activating to production, a release engineer has to answer one question: *does the site behave and look the same through staging as it does through production?* Today that is answered by hand from a regression sheet: page loads, header checks, redirects and eyeballed screenshots.

The product automates that sheet. It runs each app's test suite on a schedule or on demand against every **app × environment × Akamai network** combination. It records functional results and screenshots, and **compares** runs pairwise: staging against prod, one environment against another, or any two runs. The comparison combines deterministic functional diffs with an AI visual judge, and produces a **Go / Review / No-Go** verdict for the change.

Everything is available to signed-in users with role-based permissions, through an HTTP API and to AI assistants through an MCP server. Every action is written to an audit trail.

---

## 2. Problem statement

| Problem | Consequence today |
|---|---|
| Staging-vs-prod verification is manual | Slow, inconsistent, skipped under time pressure |
| Testing on Akamai staging means editing `/etc/hosts` per hostname | Error-prone, not reproducible, impossible to schedule |
| Screenshot comparison by eye | Misses regressions, or flags noise (carousels, ads, chat widgets) as failures |
| No history | A red test can't be classified as a regression, a flake or an environment problem |
| Several apps and environments (prod, UAT, …) | Each combination multiplies the manual work |
| Approvals happen in change tickets | There is no evidence trail of what was tested, by whom, and what the result was |

---

## 3. Goals, non-goals and success metrics

### 3.1 Goals
| # | Goal |
|---|---|
| G1 | Answer "is this Akamai staging configuration safe to activate?" per app and environment, with an evidence-backed Go/No-Go. |
| G2 | Execute an existing regression sheet unchanged in meaning, against both Akamai networks, without manual host pinning. |
| G3 | Separate real regressions from noise: deterministic functional checks plus an AI visual judge that ignores known dynamic content. |
| G4 | Let users declare known, acceptable differences once, so they stop blocking every later verdict. |
| G5 | Scale to many apps and environments through **configuration only**: no code change to add an app or an env. |
| G6 | Make every result, verdict and action attributable to a named user and auditable. |
| G7 | Make the whole product usable programmatically (API) and by AI assistants (MCP) with the same permissions. |

### 3.2 Non-goals
- A general-purpose test platform: no pluggable test types, no arbitrary dimensions or tags. The model is exactly **app → env → network**.
- Comparing runs of **different apps**, or more than two runs at once.
- Editing suites inside the product. Suites are authored as spreadsheets/CSV.
- Non-Akamai CDNs or networks.
- A database. Object storage plus small index documents is enough.
- Per-app roles (deferred, see §15).
- Automating form submits, emails and PDF downloads from the sheet. Only page loads and HTTP checks are automated.

### 3.3 Success metrics
| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Time from "start comparison" to verdict for a ~90-test suite with ~55 screenshots | ≤ 5 min (runs take ~1–2 min) |
| Verdict correctness | GO is never issued for a partial run, a run with judge errors, or a candidate with failing tests |
| False "different" visual verdicts on unchanged pages | Near zero: identical and near-identical pairs never reach the AI, and blocking verdicts are second-checked |
| Effort to add an app | One CSV plus one config entry |
| Effort to add an environment | One config line |
| Overview API latency (warm, 30 targets) | p95 < 300 ms, with no object LIST and no canary-status call per request |
| Actions attributable to a user | 100% of state-changing actions audited |

