## 4. Users and roles

### 4.1 Personas
| Persona | Need |
|---|---|
| **Release engineer** (Akamai config owner) | Has just pushed a property version to staging. Needs a Go/No-Go before activating to prod, and a summary for the change ticket. |
| **On-call / triager** | A scheduled run went red. Needs to know whether it is a real regression, a flake or an environment issue. |
| **Test author** | Iterating on one failing row of the sheet. Needs to re-run single tests and reproduce a check outside the tool. |
| **Reviewer / lead** | Needs a shareable, credential-free reference to a result, and evidence for approvals. |
| **Platform owner / admin** | Deploys the system, manages users, audits activity. |
| **AI assistant user** | Wants to ask an assistant to "compare staging with prod for CHG-1234 and tell me if it's a go". |

### 4.2 Roles
| Role | Can |
|---|---|
| **viewer** | Read everything: runs, comparisons, tests, rules, live progress, their own audit trail. |
| **operator** | Everything a viewer can, plus start, stop and queue runs; start ad-hoc comparisons; re-judge; create, toggle and delete accepted-difference rules. |
| **admin** | Everything an operator can, plus manage users and read everyone's audit trail. |
| **owner** | The holder of the deployment's master token. Acts as an admin. Used to bootstrap users and for automation. |

Roles are global: they apply to every app.

