## 5. Domain model and glossary

```
App ─┬─ Suite (one CSV; canonical hostnames; test IDs unique within the app)
     └─ Env ─┬─ host map, headers, schedules
             └─ Network: prod | staging (Akamai)
                    = Target ── Runs ── Results ── Screenshots
Comparison = (baseline Target, candidate Target, kind)    kind: network | env | adhoc
Accepted rule = (comparison, kind of difference, test?)   per app
```

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **App** | A site with its own suite and canonical hostnames, e.g. `www`. |
| **Env** | One deployment of an app. It maps the suite's canonical hosts to its own, e.g. `uat`: `www.salesforce.com` → `www-uat1.salesforce.com`. |
| **Network** | The Akamai network requests go through: `prod` (normal DNS) or `staging`. |
| **Target** | App × env × network, e.g. `www.uat.staging`. One scheduled runner and one run history. |
| **Suite** | The CSV export of an app's regression sheet. One row is one test. |
| **Run** | One execution of a target's suite, either full or a subset of tests. |
| **Result** | The outcome of one test in one run: status, headers, assertion errors, redirect chain, timing, screenshot. |
| **Comparison** | A diff of a candidate run against a baseline run, test by test. |
| **Network comparison** | Same app and env, staging (candidate) vs prod (baseline). Generated automatically. This is the release gate. |
| **Env comparison** | Same app and network, two envs, e.g. uat vs prod. Opt-in. |
| **Ad-hoc comparison** | Any two finished runs of one app. Informational, with no Go/No-Go. |
| **Item** | One test's entry in a comparison: functional diffs, visual verdict, item verdict. |
| **Version** | A re-run or re-judge produces a new version of a comparison. It is not a new comparison. |
| **Accepted rule** | A user-declared acceptable difference that stops counting towards verdicts. |
| **Pinned baseline** | A known-good baseline run chosen explicitly, so only the candidate has to run. |

### 5.1 Identifiers
- App and env names match `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,11}$`, contain no dots, and the app name `suites` is reserved.
- Target ID: `<app>.<env>.<network>`.
- Comparison IDs:
  - network: `<app>.<env>.staging-vs-prod`
  - env: `<app>.<candidate>-vs-<baseline>.<network>`
  - ad hoc: `<app>.adhoc`, one bucket per app
- Test identity is `(app, test id)`. Every API that names a test also names the app.
- Runner name: `<prefix>-<app>-<env>-<p|s>`, at most 21 characters. Two app/env pairs must never produce the same runner name.

