| FR-AUTH-1 | Users **must** sign in with their own name and password. Names are 2–64 chars of `a-z 0-9 . _ @ -` (an email works). `owner` is reserved. |
| FR-AUTH-2 | Passwords **must** be stored as salted PBKDF2-SHA256 with 600k iterations, never in clear, and never readable by the comparison service. |
| FR-AUTH-3 | **Password policy:** at least 10 characters; at most 256; must not contain the user name; a new password must differ from the old one. |
| FR-AUTH-4 | Admins create users with a role. Without an explicit password, the system **must** generate a temporary one, returned **once**. The user **must** choose their own at first sign-in, and no other action is allowed until then. |
| FR-AUTH-5 | Admins **must** be able to change a role, disable or enable a user, reset a password (new temporary password, change required), delete a user, and list users (without hashes). Admins **must not** be able to disable, delete or demote themselves. |
| FR-AUTH-6 | A sign-in **must** return a signed session token valid for 12 h. It is invalidated immediately when the user is disabled, deleted or changes password. Role changes apply within seconds, with no new sign-in. |
| FR-AUTH-7 | **Throttling.** After 5 failed sign-ins in 15 min, per name **or** per client IP, sign-in **must** be refused (429) for a while. Unknown names **must** take the same time as known ones. |
| FR-AUTH-8 | Users **must** be able to read their own profile (role, last sign-in, session expiry) and change their password. Changing it returns a fresh session. |
| FR-AUTH-9 | The deployment's master token **must** authenticate as the owner (admin). Changing it **must** sign everyone out. |
| FR-AUTH-10 | A user **must** be able to obtain their own session token and a ready-made AI-assistant configuration that carries it, so the assistant acts as them, with their role. |

